      "verdict": "protected-sample full KL = 2.3384 >= 0.01: measurable distribution drift on the samples A3 must protect -> the soft-KL constraint has signal to act on; gradient calibration: ||grad_K L_base|| = 3.514e-03 vs ||grad_K KL_prot|| = 2.435e+04 -> lambda_grad ~ 1.44e-07 as the SWEEP CENTER, not an exact equivalence (Adam rescales per-parameter updates; scan at least +-1 order of magnitude around it; the CE scalar passes no continuous gradient to the key); margin-hinge reference form (winner-preserving, NOT similarity regression): L_margin = max(0, m - s_new(x, k_old*) + max_{j != old*} s_new(x, k_j)) with old* = argmax_j s_old(x, k_j) \u2014 the slot the OLD interface chose must stay ahead of every competitor by at least m under the NEW interface",
      "a3_kl_first_version_recommendation": "detach the student-side features in the compatibility term \u2014 R_new = softmax(tau * sim(sg(z_new), K_new)) \u2014 so the KL updates ONLY the key; this matches the key-only lambda_grad calibration above (no prompt-side gradient was measured, so no prompt-update lambda can be inferred from these numbers)"
